Chapter 10
Cost-based and market-based pricing
التسعير على أساس التكلفة والتسعير على أساس السوق
Every chapter so far has taken the price as given. Chapter 1 priced a jar at $12.00, Chapter 7 asked whether to accept $8.50 for a special order, and Book 1 found that Orontes had been giving away two points of gross margin a year. None of them asked where the $12.00 came from.
It came from one of two places, and the difference between them is the subject of this chapter. A cost-based price starts inside the company, adds a margin to a cost and arrives at a number. A market-based price starts outside, with what customers will pay and what competitors charge, and works back to what the product must cost. Most companies use both, and the exam tests whether a candidate knows which question each answers.
Figure F710-01 is your map.
Figure F710-01. Chapter 10 roadmap: pricing from the inside out, and from the outside in.
